       documented by SVr4 other than its presence in a list of libtermlib.so.1
       symbols.  Reading the source code (i.e., Illumos):

       •   ssllkk__ssttaarrtt has two parameters:

           •   _n_g (number of groups) and

           •   _g_p (group pointer).

       •   Soft-key groups are an array of _n_g integers.

       •   In  SVr4, ssllkk__iinniitt calls ssllkk__ssttaarrtt passing a null for _g_p.  For this
           case, ssllkk__ssttaarrtt uses the number of groups _n_g (3 for the 3-2-3  lay‐
           out, 2 for the 4-4 layout) which ssllkk__iinniitt provided.

